(F5 T6 U3: circle grid of middles and radii: middles 3 x 3 on x 3..3.6,
 y 2.5..3.5 (x fastest), radii 0.6 and 1.1 (outer loop), 12 points per circle,
 18 surfaces. 4x4 quad4 mesh on [0,4]x[0,4], uniform strain: sigxx = sigyy = -1,
 sigxy = 0.5, Mohr-Coulomb c 1, phi 30 deg (elastic). Point at angle t on a
 circle (outward normal): sigma_n = -1 + 0.5 sin 2t, |tau| = 0.5 |cos 2t|;
 points outside the mesh do not count. The circles near the right edge lose different arcs, so
 Fs differ: surface 0 (3,2.5) r 0.6 4.7320508076, surface 8 (3.6,3.5) r 0.6
 4.7320508076, surface 17 (3.6,3.5) r 1.1 3.8729340512; critical surface
 17: middle (3.6, 3.5), r 1.1, Fs 3.8729340512.)
